.TH "REPROCTL\-UP" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-up \- bring the development environment online
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]] \f[B]up\f[R]
[\f[I]service\f[R]...]
[\f[B]\-\-wait\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bring the full development environment online with a single command.
Ensures the local kind cluster is running, then starts the requested
services via Tilt.
.PP
If no services are specified, all services defined in
\f[B]services.json\f[R] are started.
If specific services are given, only those are started.
.PP
When the cluster is already running, the cluster\-creation step is
skipped.
When Tilt is already running, the new services are merged into the
running configuration (same as \f[B]reproctl start\f[R]).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-wait\f[R]
Block until all started services report a healthy runtime status.
Times out after 300 seconds with a warning.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]
Output a JSON summary of the operation.
The object includes the command name and the list of services that were
started.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl up
Start all services (cluster is created if needed).
.TP
reproctl up api\-server workspace
Start only api\-server and workspace.
.TP
reproctl up \-\-wait
Start all services and block until healthy.
.TP
reproctl \-\-json up api\-server
Start api\-server and output JSON summary.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]reproctl\f[R](1), \f[B]reproctl\-down\f[R](1),
\f[B]reproctl\-start\f[R](1), \f[B]reproctl\-cluster\f[R](1)
